Subject: Serves register-VM named-property reads from the runtime's global stub cache

What this does
  Serves register-VM named-property reads from the runtime's global stub cache.

Why we need it
  The per-function register property cache refuses a receiver whose shape is unhashed or a holder more than one hop away, and the built-in objects are unhashed, so every read of `Math.PI`, `Number.MAX_VALUE` or a prototype method left the cache and re-walked the chain; the runtime already carried a reference-free global stub cache that only the stack VM consulted.

What it adds
  `regvm_get_field_ic` probes `js_megacache_probe` before the generic walk and `regvm_pic_fill` resolves a holder at depth 0/1/2 and calls `js_megacache_fill` exactly when the per-function cache refuses the site; a hit still requires a non-TMASK slot, because an autoinit slot holds a raw realm/id descriptor rather than a value; the cache's stale-address guard was also completed with three `rt->shape_free_epoch` bumps (`resize_properties`, `compact_properties`) and the same non-TMASK guard on the stack VM's probe.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
